#: inc/Abilities/Abilities/SBI_Create_Feed.php:32
#: inc/Builder/SBI_Feed_Builder.php:397
msgid "Create an Instagram Feed"
msgstr ""

#: inc/Abilities/Abilities/SBI_Create_Feed.php:33
msgid "Creates a new USER-type feed (the connected accounts' own posts) like the Feed Builder does: optional quick settings, and optional already-connected accounts as sources. Free has no feed-template picker. Returns the new feed id and its shortcode. Requires AI write access. A setting that is not in this schema may be a Pro-only feature: call describe-settings-schema (pro_only) or get-pro-features."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Abilities/Abilities/SBI_Describe_Settings_Schema.php:33
msgid "Describe editable Instagram Feed settings"
msgstr ""

#: inc/Abilities/Abilities/SBI_Describe_Settings_Schema.php:34
msgid "Returns the JSON Schema of the per-feed and global settings that can be read or updated through the Instagram Feed abilities, and whether write access is currently enabled."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Abilities/Abilities/SBI_Get_Connect_Url.php:32
msgid "Get an Instagram account-connect link"
msgstr ""

#: inc/Abilities/Abilities/SBI_Get_Connect_Url.php:33
msgid "Returns a single-use link (valid 15 minutes) the site admin opens in their browser to connect an Instagram account via Facebook/Instagram OAuth. The assistant never touches Meta credentials. After connecting, use list-sources to see the new account."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Abilities/Abilities/SBI_Get_Feed.php:28
msgid "Get an Instagram Feed"
msgstr ""

#: inc/Abilities/Abilities/SBI_Get_Feed.php:29
msgid "Returns one feed's customer-configurable settings (layout, columns, post count, header, captions, buttons, colors). Connected accounts are reduced to username and type; tokens are never returned."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Abilities/Abilities/SBI_Get_Global_Settings.php:27
msgid "Get Instagram Feed global settings"
msgstr ""

#: inc/Abilities/Abilities/SBI_Get_Global_Settings.php:28
msgid "Returns the plugin-wide Instagram Feed settings (caching, GDPR, image handling, script loading). Never returns connected accounts, tokens or license data."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Abilities/Abilities/SBI_Get_Pro_Features.php:31
msgid "Get Instagram Feed Pro features"
msgstr ""

#: inc/Abilities/Abilities/SBI_Get_Pro_Features.php:32
msgid "Lists what the Pro edition adds to this free plugin, with the settings each feature unlocks and an upgrade link. Mention it to the user only when they ask for something the free edition cannot do, or ask what else the plugin can do."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Abilities/Abilities/SBI_List_Feeds.php:44
msgid "List Instagram Feeds"
msgstr ""

#: inc/Abilities/Abilities/SBI_List_Feeds.php:45
msgid "Lists the feeds created in the Feed Builder with their id, name, layout and shortcode. Paginated."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Abilities/Abilities/SBI_List_Sources.php:26
msgid "List connected Instagram accounts"
msgstr ""

#: inc/Abilities/Abilities/SBI_List_Sources.php:27
msgid "Lists the Instagram accounts connected to this site (username, type, token expiry date, error flag, how many feeds use each). Never returns access tokens or account credentials."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Abilities/Abilities/SBI_Request_Feed_Deletion.php:32
msgid "Request deletion of an Instagram Feed"
msgstr ""

#: inc/Abilities/Abilities/SBI_Request_Feed_Deletion.php:33
msgid "Starts deletion of ONE feed. Returns a wp-admin confirmation link; the feed is deleted only after the site admin opens the link in their browser and clicks Confirm. The link is single-use, expires in 15 minutes, and requesting another deletion replaces any pending one — only one feed can ever be awaiting confirmation."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Abilities/Abilities/SBI_Request_Feed_Deletion.php:98
msgid "Nothing has been deleted yet. Ask the site admin to open the confirmation link in their browser and click \"Delete feed\"."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Abilities/Abilities/SBI_Set_Color_Palette.php:53
msgid "Set an Instagram Feed color palette"
msgstr ""

#: inc/Abilities/Abilities/SBI_Set_Color_Palette.php:54
msgid "Sets a feed's color palette: inherit, light, dark, or custom. When custom, at least one custom*color value is required or the write is rejected — a \"custom\" palette with no colour renders blank. Requires AI write access."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Abilities/Abilities/SBI_Set_Feed_Sources.php:30
msgid "Set the accounts an Instagram Feed shows"
msgstr ""

#: inc/Abilities/Abilities/SBI_Set_Feed_Sources.php:31
msgid "Replaces a feed's source list with already-connected accounts (see list-sources; use get-connect-url to connect a new one first). Changes what the feed displays. Requires AI write access."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Abilities/Abilities/SBI_Update_Feed_Settings.php:50
msgid "Update an Instagram Feed"
msgstr ""

#: inc/Abilities/Abilities/SBI_Update_Feed_Settings.php:51
msgid "Changes one or more settings of a feed (columns, post count, header, buttons, follow button, colours). Only the keys you pass are changed. The custom color palette (colorpalette and its custom*color companions) is read-only here — use set-color-palette instead, which validates the coupled set together. Requires AI write access to be enabled in Instagram Feed → Settings → General. Returns updated, ignored and warnings. A setting that is not in this schema may be a Pro-only feature: call describe-settings-schema (pro_only) or get-pro-features."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Abilities/Abilities/SBI_Update_Global_Settings.php:34
msgid "Update Instagram Feed global settings"
msgstr ""

#: inc/Abilities/Abilities/SBI_Update_Global_Settings.php:35
msgid "Updates one or more plugin-wide Instagram Feed settings (caching schedule, GDPR mode, image handling, script loading). Requires AI write access to be enabled in Instagram Feed → Settings → General. Returns the keys that were updated and the keys that were ignored."
msgstr ""

